WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:02.400
-Our next guest can be seen

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.767
at the New York Comedy Cellar
March 4th through the 6th.

00:00:04.767 --> 00:00:07.801
Making his "Tonight Show" debut,
please welcome the very funny

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:09.634
Eric Neumann, everybody.

00:00:09.634 --> 00:00:11.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:11.634 --> 00:00:18.200
♪♪

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.934
-Thank you.
Thank you so much.

00:00:19.934 --> 00:00:21.534
How we feeling, guys?
We good?

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.801
[ Cheers and applause ]
Oh.

00:00:23.801 --> 00:00:26.801
Oh, amazing.
I'm so happy to be here.

00:00:26.801 --> 00:00:29.567
Actually, my mom's
a very overprotective mom,

00:00:29.567 --> 00:00:32.067
so to be honest, I'm happy
to be anywhere she is not.

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:33.901
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.901 --> 00:00:36.133
She's --
She's super overprotective.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:38.567
She'll like -- She'll text me
when I'm out at night.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:41.767
She'll be like, "Call me as soon
as you leave the bar.

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:43.667
I'm worried someone's
gonna follow you home."

00:00:43.667 --> 00:00:45.601
[ Laughter ]
I'm like, "Mom, the whole point

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.767
of me going out was to get
someone to follow me home."

00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:51.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:51.133 --> 00:00:52.834
She'll call me
in the middle of the night

00:00:52.834 --> 00:00:55.367
to make sure I got home okay,
but if I don't answer the phone

00:00:55.367 --> 00:00:56.567
'cause I'm busy,
she'll call one of

00:00:56.567 --> 00:00:59.200
my best friends looking for me.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:01.067
I'm 34.
That's unacceptable.

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.534 --> 00:01:03.901
So finally, I sat her down.
I'm like,

00:01:03.901 --> 00:01:06.701
"Mom, you have to stop calling
my friends at 4:00 a.m.

00:01:06.701 --> 00:01:08.634
You're gonna give them
the wrong impression."

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:09.767
[ Light laughter ]
Right?

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.400
'Cause my friends are wasted
at 4:00 a.m.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:13.601
I don't trust them talking to
my mom on the phone at all.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.901 --> 00:01:17.133
This is how I see the scenario

00:01:17.133 --> 00:01:18.367
playing out in my head,
all right?

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:20.133
My mom calls my best friend,
Joe, at 4:00 a.m.

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:22.100
She's like,
"Hey, Joe, is Eric with you?"

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:24.901
Joe is like, "No, I'm all alone.
You want to come over?"

00:01:24.901 --> 00:01:28.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.534 --> 00:01:31.834
It's my worst nightmare.
Literally, my worst nightmare.

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:34.767
I just found out my mom and I
have the same therapist.

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.834
Which is weird.
It's weird.

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:42.167
But it's fine because he's sworn
to confidentiality.

00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:43.501
Like, he can't even
legally admit

00:01:43.501 --> 00:01:45.868
that he knows who my mom is.

00:01:45.868 --> 00:01:49.734
So sometimes, I like to test him
to see how professional he is.

00:01:49.734 --> 00:01:51.634
The other day, I was like, "Oh,
my mom's so overbearing, man.

00:01:51.634 --> 00:01:54.367
I can't take it.
She's in therapy to get help

00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:57.000
but says her therapist
is an unhelpful moron."

00:01:57.000 --> 00:02:01.133
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.133 --> 00:02:03.000
"Can't even believe
he has a degree, really."

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:04.467
[ Laughter ]

00:02:04.467 --> 00:02:06.000
He's like, "Oh, that's weird,
because I have a patient

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:07.534
whose son is a real schmuck."

00:02:07.534 --> 00:02:10.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:10.534 --> 00:02:12.734
I'm like,
"All right, touché, sir.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.567
You won that battle."

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.634
I've gotten my heart broken
so many times.

00:02:16.634 --> 00:02:18.334
So many times.

00:02:18.334 --> 00:02:21.567
I remember I dated this girl
briefly in fifth grade.

00:02:21.567 --> 00:02:25.434
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.434 --> 00:02:27.267
And I haven't seen her
since fifth grade.

00:02:27.267 --> 00:02:29.667
Last week, I ran into her
on the street, and she goes,

00:02:29.667 --> 00:02:32.234
"Hey, Eric, remember when I
broke up with you in 5th grade

00:02:32.234 --> 00:02:34.200
Because the nurse pulled you
out of the classroom

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:38.200
for having lice."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.434
I'm, like,
"You mean the most devastating

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:41.767
moment of my entire life?"
[ Laughter ]

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:45.534
"Yeah, I vaguely recall that."
I remember I was so devastated,

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.767
I came back into the classroom,
and some kid next to me

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:49.467
was like, "Eric,
why do you look so sad?"

00:02:49.467 --> 00:02:51.200
I'm like,
"Because Nadia just dumped me,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:52.734
and now I'm all alone."

00:02:52.734 --> 00:02:54.501
And I swear he pointed
at my head, and he's like,

00:02:54.501 --> 00:03:03.868
"No, you're not."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:03.868 --> 00:03:06.434
My mom really wants me
to settle down, have kids.

00:03:06.434 --> 00:03:08.834
You know, my younger brother
has a 2-year-old daughter now,

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:10.133
and everybody's like,
"Oh, now that your brother

00:03:10.133 --> 00:03:11.300
has a kid,
your mom's gonna put

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:12.834
less pressure on you
to have kids."

00:03:12.834 --> 00:03:14.367
It's not true.

00:03:14.367 --> 00:03:15.701
She doesn't put
less pressure on me,

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:18.300
she's just changed her approach.
That's all.

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:19.834
Like, the other day,
I met up with my mom

00:03:19.834 --> 00:03:21.534
and my niece,
and my niece was crying.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.834
I was like,
"Mom, why is she crying?"

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:24.334
And she goes,
"I think it's because

00:03:24.334 --> 00:03:28.834
she doesn't have a cousin."
[ Laughter ]

00:03:28.834 --> 00:03:31.968
She's a genius.
She's brilliant, that woman.

00:03:31.968 --> 00:03:34.000
I take my niece
to go get coffee every morning.

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:36.167
I take her to the coffee shop.
That's our routine.

00:03:36.167 --> 00:03:38.100
And I love doing it
for two reasons.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.801
One, she's so cute.

00:03:39.801 --> 00:03:42.200
And two,
it is so easy to pick up women.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:43.801
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:47.100
But only if I make it very clear
that she's not my daughter.

00:03:47.100 --> 00:03:48.767
So the other day,
we were at the coffee shop.

00:03:48.767 --> 00:03:50.634
Some beautiful girl passed by,
looked at my niece,

00:03:50.634 --> 00:03:52.834
and I was like,
"Can you say 'uncle'?"

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:57.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:57.968 --> 00:03:59.868
"Can you say 'single uncle'?"

00:03:59.868 --> 00:04:08.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:08.367 --> 00:04:11.133
"Who's your single uncle, huh?

00:04:11.133 --> 00:04:13.367
Who's your single uncle
who will definitely be faithful

00:04:13.367 --> 00:04:15.701
this time around
because he learned his lesson?"

00:04:15.701 --> 00:04:19.467
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.467 --> 00:04:21.634
Even my friends
are starting to worry about me.

00:04:21.634 --> 00:04:23.033
Like, the other day,
my friend goes, "Hey, Eric,

00:04:23.033 --> 00:04:25.467
you have to meet a girl
before you become rich

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:27.567
because then you'll know
she really loves you."

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:28.934
He goes, "Look at LeBron James."

00:04:28.934 --> 00:04:31.834
That was the example he used --
LeBron James.

00:04:31.834 --> 00:04:33.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.167 --> 00:04:35.200
He goes, "LeBron met his wife
in high school, right?

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.367
So you know
she really loves him.

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:39.200
She dated him before
he was LeBron James."

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:42.367
I'm like, "Yeah, but it's not
like there weren't signs."

00:04:42.367 --> 00:04:44.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.434
"Becky, you'll never guess
who just asked me out.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:48.067
You know that guy, LeBron,
who's 6'9"

00:04:48.067 --> 00:04:49.868
and averages
85 points per game?"

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:55.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:57.133
"Yeah, the one
who was on the cover

00:04:57.133 --> 00:05:00.133
of 'Sports Illustrated'
at 14 years old?"

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:01.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:03.133
"Yeah, I think I'm gonna
roll the dice on him."

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:04.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.767 --> 00:05:07.367
"I know it's a long shot.
I'm gonna go for it.

00:05:07.367 --> 00:05:10.734
I have no idea what he wants
to do for his career.

00:05:10.734 --> 00:05:15.000
I know, for fun, he likes
to hop over school buses.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.167
But for a career, who knows?"
You guys have been amazing.

00:05:17.167 --> 00:05:18.734
I'm Eric Neumann.
Thank you so much, everybody.

00:05:18.734 --> 00:05:20.567
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:20.567 --> 00:05:24.767
-That is --
That's Eric Neumann!

00:05:24.767 --> 00:05:28.434
Oh, fantastic job.
That's Eric Neumann!

00:05:28.434 --> 00:05:30.400
He'll be at
the New York Comedy Cellar

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:32.801
March 4th through the 6th.

